# Stapler Engine

A lightweight, decoupled **2.5D narrative point-and-click web game engine** built with **TypeScript** and **Three.js**, designed for visual-novel/exploration hybrids with a tactile paper-cutout diorama aesthetic.

## Project Structure

- `setup.sh` — One-step workspace installation, TypeScript typecheck, and build verification script.
- `docs/` — Plain-text-friendly documentation explaining how every part of the engine works together (`00-overview.md` through `04-extending-and-next-steps.md`).
- `packages/stapler-engine/` — Reusable decoupled TypeScript + Three.js engine (`@stapler/engine`).
- `games/paper-expressions/` — Vertical-slice test game (`@stapler/paper-expressions`).
- `Chloe.svg` & `Unua.svg` — Hand-authored Inkscape SVG style anchors (protagonist Chloe Relay in winter attire and Professor Unua).
- `tools/svg/` — Human-in-the-loop SVG inspection, rigging, sticker-border, base-NPC mannequin, and puppet-pose animation CLI toolkit (`docs/tools/svg-asset-pipeline.md`).
- `docs/software_specifications/1-Stapler_Engine.md` — Engine requirements, asset formats, rendering constraints, and test game design (*Paper expressions*).
- `docs/software_specifications/2-Architecture.md` — Technical architecture, TypeScript contracts, Tiled/dialogue schemas, and build milestones.
- `Concept Art/SVG and example character/` — Early paper-cutout visual style reference and Ada Nudos pose/walk-cycle explorations.
- `Concept Art/User Interface/` — UI and visual novel overlay mockups (planned).

## Core Technical Pillars

- **2.5D Paper-Cutout Rendering:** SVG-authored characters rasterized to high-DPI textures on lit 3D planes with alpha-cutout silhouette shadows and optional `.glb` 3D props.
- **Compact Tile Environments:** Fixed-camera rectangular environments (default budget up to `4,096` tiles / max dimension `64`) authored in Tiled (`.tmj`), with merged/chunked geometry, configurable wall heights + optional interior partitions, and configurable lights (capped at 2 shadow casters).
- **Hybrid Controls & VN Overlay:** Grid A* point-and-click (with path smoothing) + WASD/keyboard controls paired with a localized HTML/CSS visual novel dialogue overlay.
- **Web-First Discipline:** `.opus`/`.mp3` audio with Web Audio concurrency limits, `IndexedDB` configurable save slots (default 10 + autosave), explicit Three.js GPU resource disposal across scene transitions, and fast Node-only **Vitest** critical-path unit tests.

## Test Game: *Paper expressions*

A 15-minute narrative prologue set in a cooled, lightly snowy equatorial country where humans have grown scarce, following **Chloe Relay** — a sleepy android infiltrating university life — across 6 environments (apartment interior, upper/lower tower hallways, lightly snowy front road & campus, and compilers classroom) alongside classmate **Ada Nudos**, **Professor Turrialba**, and Chloe's robot creator, **Professor Unua**.
